.TH AMBER 1 "October 2026" "amber" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
amber \- ncurses client for the amber AI agent harness
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B amber
[\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B amber
is the full-screen client for the amber harness. It runs an agent loop against
an OpenAI-compatible endpoint: the model reads and writes files, searches the
project and runs commands through approval-gated tools while the session,
context and tool output are rendered in place.
.PP
Commands are typed at the prompt. A leading \fB/\fR opens a command path such as
\fB/set model\fR or \fB/get plugin\fR; the command tree, its help and its
completions all come from \fIcompletions.json\fR, so the surface shown on screen
is the surface that exists. Press \fB?\fR at any depth for the man page of that
node.
.PP
The harness reads \fIamber.conf\fR from the working directory, then the global
configuration, then the flags below. Model and context size are auto-detected
from the endpoint when the configuration leaves them unset.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-config \fIfile\fR
Read \fIKEY=VALUE\fR configuration from \fIfile\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-api\-base \fIurl\fR
OpenAI-compatible base URL, for example \fBhttp://localhost:8081/v1\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-api\-key \fIkey\fR
API key for the endpoint.
.TP
.B \-\-model \fIname\fR
Model name to request.
.TP
.B \-\-system \fIfile\fR
Markdown file holding the system prompt.
.TP
.B \-\-tools \fIfile\fR
Markdown file advertising the tool set.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-stream
Disable server-sent-event streaming.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-plugins
Start without the bundled plugins.
.TP
.B \-v, \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Print usage and exit.
.SH COMMANDS
Commands are namespaced paths from \fIcompletions.json\fR. \fB/get\fR reads state
(for example \fB/get config paths\fR), \fB/set\fR changes it, and \fB/help\fR
lists what the current node accepts. Package upgrades are performed by the
system package manager; see \fBamber-cli\fR(1) for \fBamber update\fR.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ./amber.conf
Project configuration: \fBapi_base\fR, \fBmodel\fR, \fBsystem_prompt\fR,
\fBtools_prompt\fR.
.TP
.I /usr/share/amber/completions.json
The command tree: namespaces, help, man pages, aliases and actions.
.TP
.I /usr/share/amber/keybindings.json
Key bindings. A missing file falls back to the compiled defaults.
.TP
.I /usr/share/amber/prompts/
System, tool, watch and domain prompts, including the coding library.
.TP
.I /usr/share/amber/data/
Skill shelf tables used by the skills surface.
.PP
Per-project state (sessions, settings, logs, experience, policy) lives under
\fB$XDG_STATE_HOME/amber/projects/\fI<slug>\fR\fR, not next to the binary.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B AMBER_API_BASE, AMBER_API_KEY, AMBER_MODEL
Defaults for the matching flags.
.TP
.B AMBER_WORKSPACE
Workspace root the read and write tools are confined to. Defaults to the
working directory.
.TP
.B AMBER_STREAM
Set to \fB0\fR to disable streaming.
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME, XDG_STATE_HOME, XDG_CACHE_HOME
Relocate configuration, per-project state and caches.
.SH SECURITY
The bash tool is approval-gated: a command runs only after the dialog is
accepted, and it is denied when no approval surface exists. Read and write are
confined to the workspace root. Run the agent as an unprivileged user, in a
container or a dedicated directory, against a model you trust.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR amber-cli (1),
.BR amber-bench (1)
